      "id": "m3",
      "authorId": "u-leo",
      "content": "Quick question: what's the difference between `let` and `const`?",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-11T09:30:00Z",
      "reactions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "m4",
      "authorId": "u-ava",
      "content": "`const` means the *variable* can't be reassigned. The object it points to can still change:",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-11T09:32:00Z",
      "reactions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "m5",
      "authorId": "u-ava",
      "content": "```\nconst user = { name: \"Leo\" };\nuser.name = \"Leo 2\"; // fine\nuser = {};           // TypeError!\n```",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-11T09:32:40Z",
      "reactions": []
    },
    {
      "id": "m6",
      "authorId": "u-leo",
      "content": "ohhh that makes sense, thanks!",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-11T09:35:00Z",
      "reactions": [
        {
          "emoji": "🙏",
          "userIds": [
            "u-ava"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
